# Mountain Giant

**Alignments.** Any.

Mountain Giants are hulking, musclebound behemoths - ten to twelve feet tall
and six to eight hundred pounds. Rumour has it they are the work of Doctor
Desmond Bradford at the Lone Star Genetics Complex, an attempt to bring out
humankind''s primal instincts and power. If so the experiment succeeded on some
level: they are savage, primal hunters, and one onlooker who watched three of
them fight nine Coalition soldiers described them as a cross between a raging
bull and an insane lion.

## The other half of them

For all the ferocity, the giants are astonishingly gentle and protective of
children - not only their own young but any child, and baby animals too. Stories
of a Mountain Giant appearing from nowhere, or fighting to its own death, to
save a child from a bear, wolves, monsters, bandits, a mudslide or drowning are
surprisingly numerous.

They also love dogs, often breeding them with wolves to use as hunting
companions and pets. That affection extends to mutant Dog Boys, who are among
the very few intelligent beings a Mountain Giant will not attack on sight and
will often befriend - which is another reason some people believe the giants
came out of the Lone Star Complex.

## Lore

Also known as the Man Mountain and the Mountain Behemoth. They are found mostly
in the Rocky Mountains, with perhaps another two or three hundred in the
mountains and bluffs of The Bend in Lone Star, and occasionally elsewhere - but
usually in the mountains, which is where the name comes from.
